#====================================================================
# Draft: djb/spac-style packages cross-compilation - two-stage build
#        with native bootstrap generator (bglibs 2.04)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-7324-BGLIBS-DJB-TWO-STAGE-CROSS-BUILD
trigger_tool:           make|libtool|crc-gentab|configure|clang|gcc|conan
phase:                  configure|build
error_signature:        cannot execute binary file: exec format error|crc-gentab|attempted to run the target compiler on the build machine|Generated source is out of date

severity:               2
category:               cross-compile-two-stage
match_keywords:         djb, spac, bglibs, conf-cc, conf-ld, choose, sysdeps, crc-gentab, bootstrap, native compiler, build-time generator, two-stage, libtool, ltcompile, makeshlib, cvm, ucspi

title:                  djb/spac packages fail cross compilation when Makefile rules run build-time generators as target binaries - solve with a two-stage build (native bootstrap generator run, then full target-toolchain build)

root_cause:             djb/spac-style trees (bglibs and the untroubled.org family) drive compilation through generated wrapper scripts (conf-cc/conf-ld baked into compile/ltcompile/load/makeshlib) and Makefile rules that EXECUTE build-time generators, e.g. bglibs `crc/*_table.c: crc-gentab`. Under OHOS cross compilation the generator is built for the TARGET (aarch64) and cannot run on an x86 worker (exec format error), or conversely a build-machine compiler leaks into target objects if conf-* keep a host cc. A naive `make` therefore fails or silently produces host-architecture artifacts; choose(1) runtime probes also degenerate under cross and must fall back to both-branches-compilable candidates.

affected_scope:         Any djb/spac package (bglibs, cvm, ucspi-* tools, djbdns derivatives) and generally any package whose Makefile executes build-time code generators (crc/gperf/bison style) during OHOS cross compilation. Verified instance - bglibs-2.04 (crc-gentab, six CRC lookup tables).

verification_cmd:       conan create archives/b/bglibs/2.04 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           native-bootstrap-generator-then-target-build
rec_description:        Two-stage pattern. Stage 1 (bootstrap): detect a machine-resident compiler by standard name (gcc/clang/cc via PATH probe script; never bare env CC per R33), run `make crc-gentab`-style generator targets only, execute the generator to emit the generated sources (CRC tables). Stage 2 (target): overwrite conf-cc/conf-ld (first line = target compiler from the Conan profile) so the spac wrapper scripts bake the cross toolchain, `make sysdeps.h libraries` with generator prerequisites now satisfied; keep all staging paths private to build_folder (R49/E524). Drive libtool via tool_requires (CI ships none). For choose(1) runtime probes rely on the choose contract that both branches must compile and pick at runtime via sysdeps.h. Never mark generator outputs as stale again (touch) and never run target ELFs on the build machine.
rec_command:            apply the two-stage recipe flow and rebuild with conan create archives/b/bglibs/2.04 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conanfile.py build() (_detect_native_cc/_write_djb_conf/two-stage make) in archives/b/bglibs/2.04/

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      commit-pregenerated-tables
fallback_description:   Pre-generate the tables on a native machine and ship them as patches so no generator runs at build time; simpler but the committed tables can drift from upstream regen rules and patches grow with every table change, so the in-recipe two-stage bootstrap is preferred.
fallback_command:       make crc-gentab on a native host, then package the generated crc/*_table.c as a patch
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       run target-architecture generator binaries on the build machine|hard-code /usr/local or host cc into conf-*|skip the generator and hand-write the tables in the recipe|use --build=missing to paper over the failure
forbid_1_reason:        exec-format failures and host-arch artifacts are exactly what the two-stage pattern exists to solve; baked host paths break relocatability (R49/E524) and hand-written tables diverge silently from upstream generators.
forbid_1_consequence:   CI exec format error loops, silently wrong-endian/wrong-arch artifacts, PF6 rejection of system-prefix injections.

principles:             minimal-recipe-diff, platform-agnostic-fix, real-evidence-over-assumption, relocatability-preserving
